  "description": "NIYHOW crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H36 Dy4 F4 N18 O19,4(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.583-3.979 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.52-114.15°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(OH)2(L_Schiff)4(H2O)2(NO3)2]·4MeCN·MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
